      "@id": "kt:multi-agent-systems",
      "@type": "kto:Paradigm",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Multi-agent systems",
      "skos:definition": "Systems made of several autonomous agents that interact (cooperating, debating or competing) to reach goals no single agent handles well; a classic AI subfield since the 1990s that has been revived by systems in which each agent is an LLM with its own role, tools and context.",
