    {
      "@id": "kt:dartmouth-workshop",
      "@type": "kto:Event",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Dartmouth workshop",
      "skos:definition": "An eight-week summer research meeting held at Dartmouth College in Hanover, New Hampshire, in 1956, organized by John McCarthy, Marvin Minsky, Nathaniel Rochester and Claude Shannon; its 1955 funding proposal introduced the term \"artificial intelligence\" and the event is widely treated as the founding of AI as a field.",
