      "@id": "kt:compute-governance",
      "@type": "kto:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Compute governance",
      "skos:definition": "The use of computing power (the chips, data centres and processing used to train and run AI models) as a lever for AI policy: measuring, allocating or restricting compute to gain visibility into AI development, steer it toward beneficial uses, and enforce limits on risky or malicious work.",
