      "skos:definition": "A model-compression technique that removes weights, neurons, channels or other structures judged unimportant from a trained neural network, producing a sparser or smaller model that ideally keeps the original accuracy while needing less memory and, when the sparsity pattern suits the hardware, less compute.",
