      "skos:prefLabel": "Principal component analysis",
      "skos:definition": "A linear dimensionality-reduction method that re-expresses centred data in an orthonormal basis of directions, the principal components, ordered by how much variance they capture; keeping the top k components gives the k-dimensional linear projection with the smallest squared reconstruction error.",
