      "skos:definition": "The ACL 2017 paper by Wang Ling, Dani Yogatama, Chris Dyer and Phil Blunsom that released AQuA, a dataset of about 100,000 multiple-choice algebra word problems with step-by-step natural-language rationales, and trained a sequence-to-program model that uses those rationales to guide the search for the arithmetic program behind each answer.",
