      "@id": "kt:scratchpad",
      "@type": "kto:Technique",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Scratchpad",
      "skos:definition": "A technique in which a language model is trained or few-shot prompted to write the intermediate steps of a multi-step computation (such as partial sums or a program's execution trace) into a delimited buffer before emitting its final answer, which markedly improves accuracy on algorithmic tasks.",
      "kto:domain": "prompting-and-reasoning",
