      "@id": "kt:goodharts-law",
      "@type": "kto:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Goodhart's law",
      "skos:definition": "The principle that a statistical regularity or metric tends to stop tracking what it stood for once it is used as a target for control or optimisation; in AI it describes how optimising a proxy objective too hard can make performance on the true objective worse.",
