      "@id": "kt:qlora",
      "@type": "kto:Technique",
      "skos:prefLabel": "QLoRA",
      "skos:definition": "A memory-efficient fine-tuning method that freezes a pretrained language model in 4-bit precision and trains only small low-rank adapter (LoRA) weights by backpropagating through the quantized model, so that models with tens of billions of parameters can be fine-tuned on a single GPU.",
