      "skos:definition": "The paper by Bahdanau, Cho and Bengio (arXiv 2014, ICLR 2015) that added a learned soft-alignment (\"attention\") step to the recurrent encoder-decoder, letting the decoder build a fresh context vector from all source positions at every output step instead of relying on one fixed-length sentence vector.",
